WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.350
How do you know it works?

2
00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:05.969
The Microsoft traffic profile has no
report-only mode, so the pilot group

3
00:00:05.969 --> 00:00:10.512
is the audit phase, read through the
sign-in query for five business days.

4
00:00:10.512 --> 00:00:11.612
Three measures.

5
00:00:11.612 --> 00:00:15.562
Client coverage: the device usage
summary's active device count,

6
00:00:15.562 --> 00:00:18.841
divided by Intune's count of
in-scope Windows devices;

7
00:00:18.841 --> 00:00:23.088
the guide's starting target is
ninety-eight percent after ring three.

8
00:00:23.088 --> 00:00:27.836
Sign-ins through the service: the share
of sign-ins marked as through Global

9
00:00:27.836 --> 00:00:32.662
Secure Access, for in-scope users; the
starting target is ninety-five percent.

10
00:00:32.662 --> 00:00:37.236
And source I P restoration, by Learn's
deployment guide test: a SharePoint

11
00:00:37.236 --> 00:00:42.113
sign-in shows the same I P address with
the client running and with it disabled.

12
00:00:42.113 --> 00:00:46.700
The rollback is simple: remove the ring's
group from the profile's assignment.
